Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: VM Stuck in Pending State
Problem: VM remains in pending state and doesn't start.

Solution Steps:

# Check VM status
kubectl describe vmi <vm-name>

# Look for scheduling events
kubectl get events --field-selector involvedObject.name=<vm-name>

# Verify node labels match affinity requirements
kubectl get nodes --show-labels | grep <required-label>
Issue 2: VM Scheduled on Wrong Node
Problem: VM is not respecting affinity rules.

Solution Steps:

# Verify the VM configuration
kubectl get vm <vm-name> -o yaml | grep -A 20 affinity

# Check if labels exist on nodes
kubectl get nodes --show-labels

# Restart the VM to trigger rescheduling
kubectl patch vm <vm-name> --type merge -p '{"spec":{"running":false}}'
kubectl patch vm <vm-name> --type merge -p '{"spec":{"running":true}}'
Issue 3: Anti-Affinity Not Working
Problem: VMs with anti-affinity rules are scheduled on the same node.

Solution Steps:

# Verify pod labels match anti-affinity selectors
kubectl get vmi --show-labels

# Check if there are enough nodes to satisfy anti-affinity
kubectl get nodes

# Review anti-affinity configuration
kubectl get vm <vm-name> -o yaml | grep -A 15 podAntiAffinity
